      en: "Quito, the capital of Ecuador, is situated at an elevation of 2,850 meters in the Andes Mountains, making it one of the highest capital cities in the world. Founded in 1534 on the ruins of an Inca settlement, the city possesses one of the best-preserved colonial centers in Latin America, which earned it the status of the first UNESCO World Heritage site in 1978. The historic center is characterized by magnificent churches such as the Iglesia de la Compañía de Jesús, famous for its interior decorated with gold leaf. Geographically, Quito is framed by the dramatic peaks of the Andes, including the active Pichincha volcano, whose Teleférico cable car takes tourists to over 4,000 meters. Just a few kilometers north of the city lies Mitad del Mundo, the monument located directly on the Equator line. Quito serves as the political and cultural heart of the country, blending colonial tradition with modern urbanity. The city's climate is often described as eternal spring, with mild days and cool nights throughout the year.",
